{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rdntzcy4sfdckcltou3n7iuvkyp7pynynhkjyrxxxbbuv5pxhniq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Outcome\n\n**The Rust translation is correct — `src/lib.rs` is unchanged.** Every one of the 48 differential tests agrees byte-for-byte with the C. The real bugs I found were in *my own test harness*, and both were the vacuous-pass kind that would have made this whole exercise worthless.\n\n### The two harness bugs (this is the important part)\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds a `cdylib`-only lib target.** Because the tests `dlopen` the library instead of linking it, cargo saw no dependency and skipped it. All 47 tests were passing against an 8-minute-old `.so`. I caught this only by mutation testing: **10 of 10 deliberately injected bugs went undetected**, including deleting the `NULL` guard outright. Fixed with `assert_fresh` in the harness, which compares `.so` mtime against every source file and *refuses to run* when stale (verified it fires, then clears after rebuild), plus `verify.sh` always building first.\n\n2. **libtest's progress output leaked into capture windows.** Redirecting the process-wide fd 1 while tests ran on parallel threads meant lines like `test cfg_16_bad_single ... ` landed *inside* the captured C output — surfacing as 6 bogus \"DIVERGENCE\" failures that looked like translation bugs. Fixed with `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` and a `detect_leak` that panics loudly rather than scrubbing bytes (scrubbing could hide a real mismatch).\n\n### Phase results\n\n- **A** — `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (12 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (24 rows), derived by grepping the C: it has **zero `return` statements**, no asserts, no error enums, and exactly **one** input-rejection branch (`if (line != NULL)`).\n- **B/C** — all 36 rows pass, driving all 5 exported symbols directly (not just the `driver` wrapper) with fixed-seed randomized inputs, including format-string injection, non-UTF-8 bytes, 1 MiB payloads, embedded NULs, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, out-of-range enum ints, and 1024-step interleaved sequences in single capture windows.\n- **D** — symbol diff **empty** for both debug and release; no C source was left untranslated.\n\n### One limitation I want to flag rather than bury\n\nAfter the staleness fix, 7/7 *observable* mutants are caught, but 4 escape — and they are **provably unobservable**, which I confirmed from the C side independently: `bad()`, `good()`, `driver(0)` and `driver(1)` all emit the identical bytes `0\\n`. `bad`/`good` differ only in `alloca` size (10 vs 40 bytes) and both print `data[0]`, which the copy loop always zeroes. So **no stdout-based test can prove `driver` routed to the correct branch** — the C ground truth doesn't distinguish them either. That routing is pinned by inspection instead (`if useGood != 0` ≡ `if (useGood)`), asserted as an explicit premise test that will fail if it ever becomes observable, and documented in `MUTATION.md`. Relatedly, the release linker folds `bad` and `good` to one address since the translated bodies are identical; both names remain exported and independently callable.\n\nAlso worth noting: `bad()`'s CWE-131 overflow (40 bytes through a 10-byte `alloca`) is matched *observably* — same output, same normal return — but not byte-identically in memory, since committing that UB in Rust could crash the harness nondeterministically without changing any output. That tradeoff is called out in `ERRORS.md` rather than left implicit.\n\nDeliverables: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `MUTATION.md`, `verify.sh`, `.cargo/config.toml`, and `tests/{common/mod.rs, phase_b_configs.rs, phase_c_errors.rs, phase_d_symbols.rs}`. `c_src/` is unmodified (md5s unchanged; only the instructed `build/` dir added). Note that `cargo test` alone will now *refuse* to run if the `.so` is stale — use `./verify.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_read_input_tokens":100800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":870,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b9902c5-ac39-4c9d-8a4b-6e98877203d6","uuid":"ca8a6a0e-001e-4d5c-b3c8-debd869434cc","timestamp":"2026-08-18T03:37:53.018Z"}
