lated bodies are identical; both names remain exported and independently callable.\n\nAlso worth noting: `bad()`'s CWE-131 overflow (40 bytes through a 10-byte `alloca`) is matched *observably* — same output, same normal return — but not byte-identically in memory, since committing that UB in Rust could crash the harness nondeterministically without changing any output. That tradeoff is called out in `ERRORS.md` rather than left implicit.\n\nDeliverables: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `MUTATION.md`, `verify.sh`, `.cargo/config.toml`, and `tests/{common/mod.rs, phase_b_configs.rs, phase_c_errors.rs, phase_d_symbols.rs}`. `c_src/` is unmodified (md5s unchanged; only the instructed `build/` dir added). Note that `cargo test` alone will now *refuse* to run if the `.so` is stale — use `./verify.sh`.","ttft_ms":3709,"ttft_stream_ms":3566,"time_to_request_ms":38,"type":"result","duration_ms":884158,"uuid":"e9ace67a-fa8b-475b-b2af-bf249fba174d"}
